 q(519,"numeric","Which joint-count definition is printed?","Monoarthritis 1 joint, oligoarthritis 1–4 joints, polyarthritis ≥5 joints","Monoarthritis 2 joints, oligoarthritis 5–10 joints, polyarthritis >10 joints","Monoarthritis 0 joints, oligoarthritis exactly 5 joints, polyarthritis exactly 6 joints","All definitions require only axial joints",exp="The number-of-joints branch defines monoarthritis as 1 joint, oligoarthritis 1–4 joints and polyarthritis ≥5 joints."),
 q(519,"scenario","A patient has localized point tenderness away from the capsule along the tendon line and pain mainly on active movement against gravity. Which category fits?","Periarticular arthritis","Articular arthritis","Axial spondyloarthritis","Crystal monoarthritis",exp="Periarticular disease has localized point tenderness, pain away from the joint capsule along tendon/bony prominences and painful active movement against gravity."),
 q(519,"scenario","Deep diffuse pain near the joint with painful passive and active movements plus crepitation, locking, deformity, instability or swelling points to what?","Articular arthritis","Periarticular tendinitis only","Neuropathy","Cutaneous vasculitis",exp="Articular arthritis has deep diffuse pain, pain in the vicinity of the joint, both passive and active painful movements, and additional crepitation/locking/deformity/instability/swelling."),
 q(519,"numeric","Which inflammatory arthritis feature and synovial-fluid threshold are printed?","Morning stiffness >45 minutes relieved by activity, worsened by rest, and synovial WBC >2000 cells/µL","Morning stiffness <5 minutes worsened by activity and WBC <200 cells/µL","Pain only at night with no lab changes","Synovial urate crystals as the sole differentiator",exp="Inflammatory arthritis has early morning stiffness >45 minutes, relieved with activity and worsened by rest; synovial fluid WBC >2000 cells/µL is best to differentiate inflammatory versus non-inflammatory."),
 q(519,"recall","Which structure note is printed for RA versus OA?","RA involves synovium; OA involves articular cartilage and stiffness worsens with activity","RA involves cartilage only; OA involves synovium only","Both involve only tendons","RA and OA both spare joints",exp="The note states the structure involved in RA is synovium and in OA is articular cartilage, with joint stiffness worsening with activity."),
